Package: mediaPlanR
Type: Package
Version: 2.0.0
Date: 2026-08-29
Title: Reliable Cross-Media Reach and Frequency Planning
Description: Reproducible tools for cross-media reach, contact-frequency
    distributions, target-audience metrics and budget-constrained reach
    optimization. Provides a validated media-plan data contract, exact
    Poisson-binomial calculations, Binomial, Beta-Binomial, canonical-expansion,
    Canonical Sequential, Morgensztern Sequential and Conditional Beta
    Distribution models, a Multivariate Beta-Binomial model, plus an explicitly
    scoped Negative-Binomial count approximation and effective-reach
    optimization with explicit optimality diagnostics. Methods follow
    Danaher (1991)
    <doi:10.1177/002224379102800311>, Leckenby & Rice (1986)
    <doi:10.1080/00913367.1986.10673014>, Ehrenberg (1959)
    <doi:10.2307/2985810>, Kim (2005, "A Canonical Sequential Aggregation
    Media Model", doctoral dissertation, The University of Texas at Austin),
    and Cheong (2007, "Multivariate Beta Binomial Distribution Model as a
    Web Media Exposure Model", doctoral dissertation, The University of
    Texas at Austin).
